WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.950
Here's a surprising fact.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.399
If you take your phone number,

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.909
it's possible to find another whole number

00:00:04.909 --> 00:00:07.093
bigger than zero such that multiplying

00:00:07.093 --> 00:00:09.503
the two of these results in an even bigger

00:00:09.503 --> 00:00:11.800
number consisting of just ones and zeros.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.272
What's more, if your phone number

00:00:14.272 --> 00:00:16.200
happens to end with a 1, 3, 7 or 9,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.204
it's possible to find a product like this where

00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:21.599
every single digit in the result is just a 1.

00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:23.849
This is part of a series of monthly puzzlers,

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.299
and the puzzle for you this month.

00:00:25.299 --> 00:00:27.072
is to prove why this is true.

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:29.153
What I like about this is that if you

00:00:29.153 --> 00:00:31.187
try to find the appropriate product for

00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:33.322
your specific phone number by brute force,

00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:35.322
it almost certainly is going to take you

00:00:35.322 --> 00:00:36.972
more computation than you have available.

00:00:37.172 --> 00:00:39.272
But if you understand the solution here,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.412
there's a way to be smarter about your brute

00:00:41.412 --> 00:00:43.172
force such that you actually could find it.

